      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.04-03",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Access to suitable family-planning information and services can help people achieve their desired timing and number of children. Services must be usable, voluntary and appropriate. A clinic's existence does not establish access for everyone if cost, distance or other barriers remain. Population policy should be assessed through rights and actual service conditions rather than assuming that a published target dictates private decisions.",
