      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.04-04",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Economic conditions can influence the costs and benefits households associate with raising children. Housing, childcare, education costs, job security and the opportunity cost of time can affect decisions. In some settings children contribute to household production or parents rely on family support in old age. These are contextual influences, not definitions of people's motives. Explain the stated circumstance without presenting a cultural stereotype as evidence.",
      "claim_ids": [
