    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.04-06",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Government policies can aim to slow rapid growth or support births where low fertility and ageing are concerns. Measures may include voluntary family planning, education, childcare, parental support or financial arrangements. The outcome depends on delivery, people's choices, costs and wider social conditions. A policy announcement is an input, not a measured change in births. Comparing before-and-after rates still requires attention to other influences and timing.",
      "claim_ids": [
