    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.04-08",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Japan provides a contrasting support-policy example. Japan’s 2025 White Paper on Children’s Policy describes a December 2024 childcare-policy direction emphasising suitable quality, local needs and family support. The mechanism aims to address constraints on desired childbearing, not to force an identical choice on every household. Expanded childcare support can be relevant without proving that fertility rose; employment, housing, service access and personal preferences remain part of the context.",
