    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.04-09",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Mortality can fall through safer water, sanitation, adequate nutrition, vaccination, treatment and wider public health improvements. These reduce particular exposures or improve survival under suitable conditions. The explanation should connect an intervention to the relevant pathway. Better sanitation can reduce some infectious disease transmission, while healthcare access supports prevention or treatment. Neither mechanism implies that every cause of death disappears.",
      "claim_ids": [
