      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.04-10",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Healthcare access depends on more than a building. Skilled staff, supplies, affordability, transport and timely use influence whether services improve survival. Rural or disadvantaged groups may face barriers despite a national improvement. A lower national mortality measure should therefore not be assumed to describe every community equally. Relevant age-specific or local evidence may be needed for a distributional claim.",
