    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.04-15",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A component comparison can illustrate different pathways. Population A has birth rate thirty and death rate ten per 1,000, with no net migration. B has birth rate ten and death rate twelve per 1,000 but net immigration of five per 1,000. A has natural growth of twenty per 1,000; B has natural decline of two but total growth of three per 1,000. Different component balances can therefore both produce an increasing total.",
      "claim_ids": [
