    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.04-17",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The most useful explanation therefore combines evidence without reducing it to one cause. Social opportunity, economic constraints, health conditions, policy and migration can work together or offset one another. Name the observed component changes, explain relevant mechanisms and keep the date and limits of the selected case visible. This provides a sound basis for judging consequences rather than assigning countries fixed labels from an old textbook description.",
      "claim_ids": [
