    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.04-21",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Migration policy and economic opportunities can also affect totals more quickly than births, but outcomes remain conditional on arrivals, departures and access. An invitation to recruit workers is not a count of workers who moved. A destination may need housing, fair working arrangements and services to make the opportunity usable. The population outcome should be measured after implementation rather than assumed from the policy intention.",
